# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# kids-paywall — environment variables
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

# Production database (Neon / any Postgres reachable over the Neon HTTP driver).
#
# Locally this can stay empty: the app falls back to SQLite in
# .data/paywall.sqlite and creates the table on the first purchase.
#
# On Vercel set NUXT_DATABASE_URL (Nitro maps it onto runtimeConfig.databaseUrl).
# A plain DATABASE_URL also works as a fallback, but the NUXT_ prefix is the
# one Nitro guarantees.
#
# Example:
# NUXT_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@ep-xxx.eu-central-1.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require
NUXT_DATABASE_URL=

# Where the local SQLite file lives (relative to the project root).
# NUXT_SQLITE_PATH=.data/paywall.sqlite
